    "_nine_hole_course": "Mt. Paul is a NINE-hole course. Both tees list 18 hole entries because the standard 18-hole round is two loops of the same nine — verified 2026-07-25: holes 1-9 and 10-18 are identical in par and yardage. Hole N and hole N+9 are the SAME PHYSICAL HOLE played twice. Stroke index is the exception and is correctly distinct across all 18 (front 5,13,11,3,17,1,15,7,9 / back 6,14,12,4,18,2,16,8,10) — that is normal for a nine played twice, so handicap strokes allocate one loop at a time. Consequence for Analytics: anything keyed on holeNum 1-18 is reporting each physical hole twice. Aggregate on ((holeNum - 1) % 9) + 1 for per-hole analysis; keep 1-18 only when the two loops are deliberately being compared (e.g. does the second nine score worse).",
    "_tees_comment": "Blue and Red are PHYSICAL tee boxes. Mt. Paul rates both for men and for ladies off the same boxes, so tees.male and tees.female carry identical par, yardage and index — only course_rating and slope_rating differ. Yardage is a property of the tee; rating is a property of the tee AND the player. Filled 2026-07-26; tees.female was an empty array before, which read as missing data when nothing was actually missing."
