    "elevation": {
      "_comment": "Elevation above sea level across the property, recorded 2026-07-25. A RANGE, not a point: the course falls roughly 70 ft from its high side to its low. Kept here rather than on the round record because it never varies between rounds — unlike tempC/windKmh, which are captured per round. Why it is recorded at all: thinner air at altitude increases carry, commonly reckoned at roughly 2% per 1,000 ft, so ~2% here. That is a constant offset for every round played at Mt. Paul, which means it explains nothing about variation BETWEEN rounds — it only matters when comparing Mt. Paul against a course at a different elevation.",
